call ar_plants_snowy x=20 z=72 r=14 seed=26498
call ar_plants_snowy x=-64 z=-8 r=24 seed=26499

# ===== Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest (19 steps) =========================================================
info title=The Sunken Liner
info author=Custom Islands
info description=Icy rocks in a cold sea, and between them on the sea floor a great liner broken in two: her ballroom still holds a breath of air, her purser's safe the Polar Star sapphire - and something with lamps lives in her stern. Lifeboat 7's survivors left a log on the biggest rock.
island on.arrive=message||Black rocks rimed with ice. On the biggest, a lifeboat drawn up and a cairn. Under the water between them, a shape too long to be a rock.

story stewardkey|Chief steward's key|quest:Vasagatan_BlueKey|The chief steward's key ring, from lifeboat 7's camp chest: it opens his cabinet in the ballroom.
story pursercode|Purser's combination|quest:Vasagatan_FourDigitCode|A card in an envelope marked PURSER - DO NOT OPEN: the combination of the purser's safe.
story sapphire|The Polar Star|Placeable_GiantClam|The Polar Star, the sapphire the whole voyage was about - blue as deep ice.
story paykey|Pay chest key|quest:Vasagatan_GreenKey|The key to the ship's pay chest, from the purser's safe.

note survivorslog Survivors' log | LIFEBOAT 7 - REGINA BOREALIS\n\nNight of the 9th. She struck the ice-rocks off these islets at full speed and broke in two. Eleven of us in lifeboat 7.\nDay 3. The chief steward died of the cold. His keys are in the camp chest - the one for his cabinet in the ballroom, where he kept the purser's safe combination "away from the purser".\nDay 5. The purser's safe holds the Polar Star, the sapphire the whole voyage was about, and the key to the ship's pay chest.\nDay 7. Smoke on the horizon - a whaler. We're going.\n\nIf anyone comes after: the wreck lies below the islets, bow toward the lifeboat, stern in the deep. Something lives in the stern now. It has lamps.
note campchest Lifeboat 7's camp chest | The survivors' chest: blankets, a flare pistol (empty) - and the chief steward's key ring.
loot campchest story:stewardkey*1;Wool*3;Rope*2
prop campchest loot.refill=0
note wireless Wireless operator's last message | CQD CQD - REGINA BOREALIS - STRUCK ICE-ROCK - BREAKING UP - POSITION ... (the rest is a water stain)\n\n(in pencil underneath) Captain says the ballroom ceiling will hold air the longest. If you are reading this under water, go there to breathe.
note stewardcab Chief steward's cabinet | The chief steward's cabinet: table silver, the last night's menus - and an envelope marked PURSER - DO NOT OPEN.
loot stewardcab story:pursercode*1;Glass*2
prop stewardcab loot.refill=0
prop stewardcab if.open=has|story:stewardkey|1
prop stewardcab else.open=message||The steward's cabinet is locked. The survivors' log said his keys are in the camp chest.
note pursersafe Purser's safe | The purser's safe: a velvet box with the Polar Star in it - and the key of the ship's pay chest.
loot pursersafe story:sapphire*1;story:paykey*1
prop pursersafe loot.refill=0
prop pursersafe if.open=has|story:pursercode|1
prop pursersafe else.open=message||A safe with a combination dial, dead still under the water. The combination was kept "away from the purser".
note paychest Ship's pay chest | The ship's pay chest: the crew's wages for a voyage that never ended, the captain's spare hat, crystal from the first-class bar - and the plans of a salvage diver's lamp somebody tucked in on the last night.
loot paychest Blueprint_HeadLight*1;Hat_Captain*1;TradeToken*15;Glass*6;MetalIngot*6
prop paychest loot.refill=0
prop paychest if.open=has|story:paykey|1
prop paychest else.open=message||The pay chest is bound in iron with one big lock. Its key is in the purser's safe.
note trunk1 First-class steamer trunk | A steamer trunk: furs ruined by the sea, a silver hairbrush, buttons.
loot trunk1 Wool*2;Leather*2;Glass*2
prop trunk1 loot.refill=0
note trunk2 Third-class trunk | A plain trunk tied with rope: work clothes, a tin of biscuits, a carpenter's tools.
loot trunk2 Rope*2;Nail*8;Hinge*1
prop trunk2 loot.refill=0
note stores Ship's stores crate | A crate from the ship's stores: tins, bolts, sheets of brass.
loot stores Bolt*4;CopperIngot*2;Cooked_GenericMeat*2
prop stores loot.refill=0
note coalbarrel Coal barrel | A barrel from the bunkers, still half full: coal, and a stoker's scrap.
loot coalbarrel Scrap*3;MetalOre*2;Stone*4
prop coalbarrel loot.refill=0
note isletbox Box in the cleft | A box wedged in a cleft of the second islet: someone from lifeboat 7 hid their things here.
loot isletbox Plank*5;Rope*2;PlasticBottle_Water*2
prop isletbox loot.refill=0

prop lifeboat zone.id=lifeboat
prop lifeboat zone.radius=7
prop lifeboat zone.message=Lifeboat 7, drawn up on the rock. A tarp, a dead fire, two deck chairs from a ship that isn't there any more.
prop bow zone.id=bow
prop bow zone.radius=10
prop bow zone.message=The bow of the Regina Borealis, upright on the sea floor as if she were still sailing - into the sand.
prop ballroom zone.id=ballroom
prop ballroom zone.radius=6
prop ballroom zone.message=The ballroom: a piano in the silt, a chandelier on the floor - and under the ceiling, a silver pocket of air.
prop ballroomair zone.id=ballroomair
prop ballroomair zone.radius=3
prop ballroomair zone.repeat=1
prop ballroomair zone.air=1
prop ballroombubbles atmo.particles=bubbles
prop ballroombubbles zone.radius=3
prop stern zone.id=stern
prop stern zone.radius=12
prop stern zone.message=The stern, raised on its bank in the dark - and two lamps turning towards you out of it.
prop purser zone.id=purser
prop purser zone.radius=5
prop purser zone.message=The purser's office, fallen from the stern and half buried in silt. His safe sits in the corner.
prop deeplamps creature.count=2
prop deeplamps creature.size=1.4
prop deeplamps creature.health=2
prop deeplamps creature.respawn=0
prop deeplamps creature.zone=stern
prop wreckdark atmo.fog=#0e2a3a
prop wreckdark atmo.fogAmount=0.6
prop wreckdark atmo.light=#1a3a4a
prop wreckdark atmo.lightAmount=0.6
prop wreckdark zone.radius=28
prop creaks sound.event=event:/amb/wreck_creaks
prop creaks sound.volume=0.6
prop creaks zone.radius=30
prop wind sound.event=event:/amb/temperance
prop wind sound.volume=0.4
prop wind zone.radius=25

story sl_top|Lookout's spyglass|Bolt|The lookout's brass spyglass, still in its box in the crow's nest.
story sl_cave|Lamp carbons|Bolt|A tin of carbon rods for the signal lamp, carried into the cave by a survivor.
story sl_fixed|Signal lamp working|Bolt|The signal lamp, working again.
note sl_hint Lookout's message | THE SIGNAL LAMP IS DARK. It wants its carbons (a survivor took them to Frost Cave, the ice cave below the rocks) and a lookout to aim it: my spyglass is still up the foremast on top of Ice Crown. - N. Ekholm, lookout
note sl_topchest Liner's fallen foremast box | A box lashed to the top of the liner's fallen foremast.
loot sl_topchest story:sl_top*1;Rope*2;Scrap*2
note sl_cavechest Frost Cave chest | A chest at the back of Frost Cave, dry under the rock.
loot sl_cavechest story:sl_cave*1;Nail*6;Plank*3
note sl_rewnote Lookout's log | The lamp flares and its beam sweeps the ice-rocks. In its hood, the lookout's log: 'Ice ahead, I rang three times. They said the bell was a drill. Nobody slowed.'
note sl_rewchest Signal lamp reward | What the signal lamp kept.
loot sl_rewchest CopperIngot*2;Bolt*3;Rope*2
note sl_lampchest Ekholm's sea chest | Ekholm's sea chest behind the hut: his watch coat, a tin of biscuits and his pay.
loot sl_lampchest Leather*2;TradeToken*2;Rope*2
note sl_setchest Steward's linen chest | A steward's chest that floated ashore: every deck chair plate back, and the first-class silver.
loot sl_setchest MetalIngot*2;Glass*3;Bolt*4
note sl_planecrate Catcher boat's locker | The whale catcher's locker: rope, a harpoon line and a crate of tinned fish.
loot sl_planecrate Rope*3;Scrap*3;Nail*6
prop sl_planecrate loot.refill=0
note sl_pilot Catcher's log | WHALE CATCHER SKUA. Came to look for survivors of the liner. Found the ice-rocks first. Aground on the far shoal, crew to the boats.
note jcsl Floe stack | Ice floes, stacked by the winter storms. A survivor left a bundle half way.
loot jcsl Rope*3;Plank*4;MetalIngot*1
note jbsl Top of the stack | A tin box on the highest floe.
loot jbsl CopperIngot*1;Bolt*2;TradeToken*1

quest title=The Polar Star
quest intro=Ice-rocks in a cold sea, a lifeboat drawn up on the biggest, and a great ship on the sea floor between them. Start at the lifeboat.
step reach|lifeboat|1|Climb onto the icy islet where lifeboat 7 came ashore
step read|Survivors' log|1|Read the survivors' log in the lifeboat camp
step collect|story:stewardkey|1|Take the chief steward's key ring from the camp chest
step reach|bow|1|Dive to the liner's bow on the sea floor
step read|Wireless operator's last message|1|Read the last message by the wireless set on the bow's deck
step reach|ballroom|1|Swim into the torn-off ballroom and breathe under its ceiling
step collect|story:pursercode|1|Open the steward's cabinet in the ballroom for the purser's combination
step kill|Angler fish|2|Drive the two lamps out of the stern
step reach|purser|1|Find the purser's office beside the stern
step collect|story:sapphire|1|Open the purser's safe for the Polar Star
step read|Lookout's message|1|Read the lookout's message by the signal lamp at the ruined house
step talk|Nils Ekholm|1|Talk to Nils Ekholm at the ruined house
step reach|sl_trail|1|Find the foot of the trail up Ice Crown, the big ice hill
step reach|sl_summit|1|Climb the trail to the top of Ice Crown
step collect|story:sl_top|1|Climb the liner's fallen foremast and take the lookout's spyglass from its box
step reach|sl_cave|1|Find Frost Cave, the ice cave under the rocks
step collect|story:sl_cave|1|Take the lamp carbons from the chest at the back of the cave
step read|Lookout's log|1|Bring both to the signal lamp and read what it shows
step open|Ship's pay chest|1|Open the ship's pay chest with the purser's key
step blueprint|Blueprint_HeadLight|1|Take the headlamp plans from the ship's pay chest
quest done=The Polar Star is yours, and the ship's last wages. Above you the ice-rocks stand where they always stood; below, the Regina Borealis sleeps on.
quest reward=OxygenBottle*2;Wool*4;MetalIngot*6

# SILVER 10-26 ground fixes: rocks the new terrain left floating (or buried) taken away, each by its spot and name
clear at 32.7 30.3 r=1.5 all only=^TP_BigRock04

save The Sunken Liner
